I really can't claim to be advanced, but I can give you some advise. Soon you
will run into a castle with a draw bridge. I know because  
I was just at that level. Sure enough, I got across, but made a fatal 
mistake:

Spoiler Follows:

It turns out that this castle was chock full of nasties. Having great armor, 
AC -8 gray dragon scale mail, amulet of life saving, rust-proof helm of
telepathy, speed boots, rustproof gaunlets of power, Aiuchi, ( a katana which
basically is the same as Stormbringer, for serious Samurai fans)  I figured 
that I was invincible. Well, this was a typical case of pride goeth before
the fall, because I was surrounded by Liches, who incapacitated me enough
to drain a total of 2x 110 hit points. Ouch! The moral of the story: Don't get 
cocky! Also, genociding liches is not a bad idea.

More Spoilers:

I have added two new artifacts to my game: Aiuchi, a katana who is patterned
after Stormbringer and Narsil, a longsword whose attack is similar to
Excaliber, but has the same warning properties of Sting. The name Aiuchi
was given to the sword by my roommate, a big Aikido buff, and Narsil was the
name of the reforged sword of Aragorn, whose name means "Flame of the West".
These are easy to create by editing artifact.c and uhitm.c . Aiuchi hits
with the response "The silver blade sucks the life out of Monster". I hope
to change this to a suitable Japanese phrase, so suggestions are welcomed.

Incidentally, I have tried to keep to the spirit of the game when editing. 
At first, I gave everyone a great wand of wishing, but found that the fun
of nethack is in succeeding even though you expect not to make it the whole
time.  
